From: Loïc Vigneron <loic@spin42.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: monaco-arduino-monza: Tell the MCU that Linux is up

Arduino's loader on the STM32H5 plays a boot animation on the LED matrix
and does not start the sketch until GPIO 95, wired to its PG13, goes
high.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
@@ -595,6 +595,17 @@
 		line-name = "WLAN_EN";
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Tells the MCU's loader that Linux is up: it plays the boot animation
+	 * on the LED matrix and holds the sketch until this line is high.
+	 */
+	mcu-mpu-booted-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <95 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+		line-name = "MCU_MPU_BOOTED";
+	};
+
 	pcie0_default_state: pcie0-default-state {
 		wake-pins {
 			pins = "gpio0";
